---
// Component: AudienceCards
// Highlights the three primary audiences: Friends & Family, Teams, and Development Teams
---

<div class="audience-cards-grid">
  <!-- Audience 1: Friends & Family -->
  <div class="audience-card">
    <div class="audience-card__icon-badge audience-card__icon-badge--family" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m3 9 9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/><polyline points="9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22"/></svg>
    </div>
    <h3>Friends & Family</h3>
    <p class="audience-card__lead">Collaborate on everyday decisions, travel, and personal spaces with AI the whole group can use.</p>
    <ul class="audience-card__list" role="list">
      <li><strong>Vacation & Trip Planning:</strong> Research destinations, compare hotel rates, and build day-by-day itineraries together.</li>
      <li><strong>Major Purchases & Comparisons:</strong> Compare appliances, vehicles, or schools and ask a second AI for another opinion.</li>
      <li><strong>Household Spaces:</strong> Organize renovations, contractors, recipes, and family budgets in separate Threads.</li>
      <li><strong>One setup for everyone:</strong> One person connects their computer; the rest of the family joins from a browser.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="audience-card__cta">
      <a href="/use-cases/#family" class="link-arrow">Explore family use cases <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Audience 2: Teams & Companies -->
  <div class="audience-card">
    <div class="audience-card__icon-badge audience-card__icon-badge--teams" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4.5 16.5c-1.5 1.26-2 5-2 5s3.74-.5 5-2c.71-.84.7-2.13-.09-2.91a2.18 2.18 0 0 0-2.91-.09z"/><path d="m12 15-3-3a22 22 0 0 1 2-3.95A12.88 12.88 0 0 1 22 2c0 2.72-.78 7.5-6 11a22.35 22.35 0 0 1-4 2z"/><path d="M9 12H4s.55-3.03 2-4c1.62-1.08 5 0 5 0"/><path d="M12 15v5s3.03-.55 4-2c1.08-1.62 0-5 0-5"/></svg>
    </div>
    <h3>Teams & Companies</h3>
    <p class="audience-card__lead">Keep team discussion, AI research, and the final decision in one place.</p>
    <ul class="audience-card__list" role="list">
      <li><strong>Collaborative Research:</strong> Synthesize industry reports, analyze competitor strategies, and summarize market data.</li>
      <li><strong>Shared Content & Strategy:</strong> Draft product specs, sales proposals, marketing campaigns, and investor memos together.</li>
      <li><strong>Multi-Model Perspectives:</strong> Compare answers from ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini in a single Thread.</li>
      <li><strong>Roles per Space:</strong> Decide who can ask the AI, who can only read, and who manages the Space.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="audience-card__cta">
      <a href="/use-cases/#teams" class="link-arrow">Explore team use cases <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Audience 3: Development & Engineering Teams -->
  <div class="audience-card">
    <div class="audience-card__icon-badge audience-card__icon-badge--dev" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="16 18 22 12 16 6"/><polyline points="8 6 2 12 8 18"/></svg>
    </div>
    <h3>Software & Technical Teams</h3>
    <p class="audience-card__lead">Run coding agents on your own machines, with tests and review recorded where the whole team can see them.</p>
    <ul class="audience-card__list" role="list">
      <li><strong>Coding agents in the Thread:</strong> Send tasks to Codex CLI, Claude Code, or Antigravity CLI on a connected machine.</li>
      <li><strong>One change at a time:</strong> Syntila queues tasks that change files so two runs do not edit the same project folder at once.</li>
      <li><strong>Automated Review & Evidence:</strong> Check code changes with test runs, diffs, and review by a second model.</li>
      <li><strong>Your machines:</strong> Repositories, toolchains, and provider logins stay on the laptop or server you connect.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="audience-card__cta">
      <a href="/use-cases/#engineering" class="link-arrow">Explore engineering use cases <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
